// Joining is similar to branching.
// The incoming sequence flow declares a "jump" by
// using an arrow `->` with a custom identifier, `join`
// in this example.
# Start 1 ->join

// This is rather similar, but with an additional
// edge display text.
# Start 2 ->join With Edge Text

// This gateway says that some sequence flows are incoming,
// with the matching `->join` attribute.
X <-join
. End
